{
  "id": "backward-masking",
  "term": "backward masking",
  "definition": "Backward masking is a visual research method in which a briefly shown target image is quickly followed by another image, called a mask, to reduce or disrupt awareness of the target. It is used to study conscious and unconscious visual processing by changing the timing between the target and the mask.",
